Well-being is an important concept in psychology that refers to a person’s overall happiness, health, and life satisfaction.
It includes emotional, mental, and social well-being. People with good well-being usually feel positive, manage stress 
effectively, and maintain healthy relationships. Regular exercise, proper sleep, a balanced diet, and spending time with 
family and friends can improve well-being. Positive thinking and self-care also help people cope with daily challenges. 
The purpose of studying well-being is to understand how people can lead happier and healthier lives. Good well-being 
contributes to personal growth and better mental health.Well-being is an important concept in psychology that refers to a
